cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the foundational paper as below. This is an unrefereed preprint; see README for caveats."
title: "KMS state uniqueness and phase transitions in localized Bost-Connes systems: from Chebotarev density to the Hardy-Littlewood conjecture"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Ruqing
    email: ruqing@hotmail.com
    affiliation: "GUT Geoservice Inc., Montreal, Canada"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add before depositing
year: 2026
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22152101"
abstract: >-
  A classification of the KMS states of the S-local Bost-Connes system over an
  arbitrary number field, for every set S of finite primes and every inverse
  temperature, in terms of an obstruction group defined by a Dirichlet series
  condition on Frobenius classes. Uniqueness is a Chebotarev-type equidistribution
  criterion; divergence of the partition function does not suffice.
keywords:
  - Bost-Connes system
  - KMS states
  - phase transitions
  - Chebotarev density theorem
  - class field theory
  - operator algebras
  - Kakutani dichotomy
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ruqing1963/localized-bost-connes"
